From: pedro <pedrocarvs26-ops@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soong: let target_init_vendor_lib exclude sources

The vendor init library cannot actually override
vendor_load_properties() while libinit still compiles the weak stub
next to it, because the two definitions land in the same archive and
the linker takes whichever member comes first.  Allow the Android.bp
side to drop the stub from libinit's sources when the variable is set.

exclude_srcs is already part of several AOSP product variables
(Product_is_iot, Arc), so nothing else is needed to support it.
---
 build/soong/android/variable.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/build/soong/android/variable.go b/build/soong/android/variable.go
--- a/build/soong/android/variable.go
+++ b/build/soong/android/variable.go
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 		Cppflags []string
 	}
 	Target_init_vendor_lib struct {
+		Exclude_srcs      []string
 		Whole_static_libs []string
 	}
 	Target_needs_netd_direct_connect_rule struct {

